{
  "dom_id": "step-q328248",
  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "Consider the following trigonometric equation: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}\u2061(6x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})=1\n$$\n\n  \n\nThe general solution of this equation can be expressed as \n\n$$\nx=a\\pi +\\frac{n\\pi }{6},\n$$\n\n \nwhere $n$ is any integer. Find a possible value of $a$ in the range $[0,\\frac{1}{6}).$\n\n$a=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "The general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6x-\\frac{\\pi }{4} & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}+n\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the above equation for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6x & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}+\\frac{\\pi }{4}+n\\pi  \\\\ 6x & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi  \\\\ x & =\\frac{\\pi }{12}+\\frac{n\\pi }{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that $a=\\frac{1}{12}.$",
